<section class="process" id="process" data-scene="code" data-process>
  <div class="process-panel">
    <div class="process-inner">
      <div class="process-head">
        <p class="section-label">(02) How it works</p>
        <h2 class="process-title" data-split>Four passes.<br /><em>No</em> guesses.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="process-steps">
        <li class="process-step" data-step>
          <span class="step-index">01</span>
          <h3>Static triage</h3>
          <p>
            Reads Python, JavaScript and TypeScript and runs none of it. Maps where request input
            and model output can reach a shell, a file, SQL or a tool.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="process-step" data-step>
          <span class="step-index">02</span>
          <h3>Source review</h3>
          <p>
            A bounded AI review reads the files on those paths, in any language, and flags each
            candidate with the lines that raised it.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="process-step" data-step>
          <span class="step-index">03</span>
          <h3>Second review</h3>
          <p>
            A separate pass plays the skeptic. It rereads the cited code with its imports and
            callers, and every dismissal shows its reasons and its lines.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="process-step" data-step>
          <span class="step-index">04</span>
          <h3>Fix prompt</h3>
          <p>
            Pick a finding and get a ready prompt for your coding agent. Plenger writes the
            prompt. You make the call.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="process-progress" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="process-progress-label">Scanning</span>
        <span class="process-progress-track"><span data-process-bar></span></span>
        <span class="process-progress-value" data-process-value>000</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
